<title>SOUTH AFRICA: PAG yr shr surges, to award cap shares.</title>
<headline>PAG yr shr surges, to award cap shares.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     26.2	  vs 13.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   10.11	 vs 3.13</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   13.35	 vs 4.92</p>
<p>    Tax			 5.32	  vs 1.79</p>
<p>    Interest received     3.58	  vs 0.23 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  136.68	vs 87.86</p>
<p>Full name: PAG Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  2.07	  vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said it would not be paying a dividend as the firm was in an expansionary phase but would be awarding capitalisation shares, the terms of which would be published on April 21.</p>
<p>They said they viewed the future with optimismand had budgeted for positive growth in the current financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
